00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.697
but we just don't seem to age, Mario.

00:00:09.697 --> 00:00:11.155
(Mario Laughing)

00:00:11.155 --> 00:00:13.745
- You're very sweet.
- No, I am, but you aren't.

00:00:13.745 --> 00:00:14.578
What's in the water?

00:00:14.578 --> 00:00:15.940
Like what are you?

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.070
- No you know, I don't know,

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.110
I just, that you're very nice, by the way.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.450
I've got really oily skin,

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.870
I'm like, if you took a
piece of fried chicken

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.000
and just wiped it on my face.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.383
- [Kelly] Look you're the same.

00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:25.640
You're the same.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.170
- Oh my gosh. I don't even--

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.430
- Hashtag! We should start a
hashtag we can't stand you.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.043
- Oh, that's funny.

00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:33.490
- It's not fair, it's crazy.

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:34.323
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:34.323 --> 00:00:35.355
When was that?

00:00:35.355 --> 00:00:36.188
Oh, that's 2000.

00:00:36.188 --> 00:00:37.061
Oh wow.

00:00:37.061 --> 00:00:38.675
Wow, that's almost 20 years ago.

00:00:38.675 --> 00:00:39.875
Oh my God,

00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:40.708
- [Kelly] Don't brag.

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:41.541
Now it's bragging!

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.224
- I didn't realize it.

00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:45.330
- I mean you could pull
up a picture from Idol

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.144
and it's, well it's real different, Mario.

00:00:47.144 --> 00:00:48.540
- I was there.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.590
I saw you a couple times.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.340
I remember, I was there when
you did, it's funny cause

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.420
I remember I was in the
audience, you did "Walk On By".

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.390
It was Burt Bacharach night.
- I did!

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:56.223
- You killed it too.

00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:57.292
- He was kind of a little upset

00:00:57.292 --> 00:00:58.560
cause I was supposed to do
"Anyone Who Had a Heart".

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.240
And then at the last minute
we were just so tired.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.300
And my voice was so tired.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.713
- You killed that.

00:01:03.713 --> 00:01:04.638
I loved that one, yes.

00:01:04.638 --> 00:01:05.471
- I gotta do this other one, but I love it

00:01:05.471 --> 00:01:06.304
cause Aretha had done it

00:01:06.304 --> 00:01:07.379
and I love Aretha.

00:01:07.379 --> 00:01:08.708
You remembered that!
- I just remembered I was in

00:01:08.708 --> 00:01:09.541
the audience for that.

00:01:09.541 --> 00:01:10.890
Fun fact.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.370
- Well now, okay, you're
hosting Access now,

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.037
and you've transitioned from Extra.

00:01:16.037 --> 00:01:17.147
So what's that like?

00:01:17.147 --> 00:01:18.179
- Yeah, I'm so excited to
be part of the NBC family.

00:01:18.179 --> 00:01:21.038
And yeah we've got Access Hollywood,

00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:23.790
Access Daily and All Access.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.206
And what's cool about it is

00:01:25.206 --> 00:01:27.510
we're the only show that goes live.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.168
So we're giving you the latest up

00:01:29.168 --> 00:01:30.770
to the minute headlines.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.350
Whatever's going on in the
world of entertainment.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.530
Literally as it's happening.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:34.920
Going live all over.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.410
There's such an energy to that

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:37.949
and it's obviously incredibly topical.

00:01:37.949 --> 00:01:39.590
But it's a great team over there

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.010
and we're having a lot of fun.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.237
And then--

00:01:42.237 --> 00:01:43.690
- It's hard to be live all the time.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.540
- Yeah it's fun.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.270
And then you know when
you're getting done though.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.020
You know when you're getting done.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.860
But then during the day too
it's cool cause we focus on,

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.447
I always say civilians, like real people.

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:54.760
Human interest stories.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.170
Sorta like what People
magazine was back in the day.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.580
And what's important to a lot of moms

00:01:58.580 --> 00:01:59.413
out there and families.

00:01:59.413 --> 00:02:00.521
I mean, I got three kids.

00:02:00.521 --> 00:02:03.820
My other co-host has three kids as well.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.730
And I know you got four. And
so, balancing life and work.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:07.626
So I'm just, I feel very blessed.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.280
And having a great time doing it.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.530
- It is a balance though, when
you have all those kiddos,

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.751
and you're married.
- It really is.

00:02:13.751 --> 00:02:16.040
And the kids have, my
kids, their activities,

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.000
their schedules are busier than mine.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.833
- I know.

00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:20.660
- You know what I mean.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.992
It's crazy
- And I like to keep them busy

00:02:22.992 --> 00:02:23.825
cause I don't want them to get in trouble.

00:02:23.825 --> 00:02:24.870
- That was my mom's philosophy with me.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.250
She put me in, that's why
I was the only dancing,

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.930
karate, wrestler, theater kid I knew.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:30.763
Every day.

00:02:30.763 --> 00:02:31.750
Cause growing up in Chula Vista

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.090
wasn't exactly the most
upscale neighborhood.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.120
There was a lot potential
to get in trouble.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:34.990
So she kept me busy.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.580
I didn't have time to get trouble.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.700
- I feel like everything you
say about yourself just makes

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.670
you cooler than all of us.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.447
Every time you open your mouth.

00:02:40.447 --> 00:02:41.820
I'm like wait, what.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.540
I was like, you took dance?

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.510
That must have been a
cool thing for chicks.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.776
They were like, "Oh hey he dances".

00:02:46.776 --> 00:02:50.530
- To be honest I got teased a lot.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.830
Cause I was usually the only boy.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:56.176
So yeah thank God--

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.010
- That's why my husband
became a cheerleader.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.890
So he could be the only guy.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.340
He was like, "I'll lift you up".

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.280
- That's funny.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.540
But that's why I was also wrestling and

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.500
doing everything else too.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.610
But I didn't want to quit
because you know, it cost money.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:09.883
And for my mom, I didn't
want to disappoint my mom.

00:03:09.883 --> 00:03:11.440
And let her down.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.940
And then I'm glad I didn't
cause then I found out

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.480
that women like guys
that know how to move.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.096
- Exactly, we all did.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.189
- So it worked out (laughs)

00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:22.283
- So how is your brand new
baby? You have a brand new baby.

00:03:22.283 --> 00:03:23.667
You have two older ones.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:28.016
- Yes I have Gia, and
Dominic, and Santino.

00:03:28.016 --> 00:03:29.650
Yeah he's like brand new.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:30.483
He's so chill.

00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:33.030
He's my most chilled out baby, so far.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:33.863
- [Kelly] So far.

00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:35.440
- That's the first day
of school right there.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.147
So the two kids, Gia
and Dominic, are going

00:03:37.147 --> 00:03:37.980
to the same school.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.176
I love that they get to wear uniforms too.

00:03:39.176 --> 00:03:40.009
Isn't that the best?
- Me too.

00:03:40.009 --> 00:03:41.270
- Mine just started school.

00:03:42.429 --> 00:03:44.140
Cause it's hell deciding
on, cause with a girl--

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.081
- And then you don't have to worry about

00:03:46.081 --> 00:03:47.381
keeping up with the Joneses and stuff.

00:03:47.381 --> 00:03:48.322
It's just like that's what
you're wearing and that's that.

00:03:48.322 --> 00:03:49.155
- Wait, my daughter doesn't do that.

00:03:49.155 --> 00:03:49.988
She's just like Punky Brewster.

00:03:49.988 --> 00:03:52.150
She likes to put everything on

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:52.983
and it's all mismatched.

00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:54.320
And my nanny wants to kill herself.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.474
Yeah, I'm fine with it.

00:03:55.474 --> 00:03:57.100
- It's one less thing to worry about.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.233
- But my nanny is always like, "Oh My God,

00:03:59.120 --> 00:03:59.977
I have to walk in with that".

00:04:00.923 --> 00:04:01.759
- Right, exactly.

00:04:01.759 --> 00:04:02.909
- You know, but I love that.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.575
That's so awesome. But
you posted a video telling

00:04:04.575 --> 00:04:07.050
your older kids that they
were getting a baby brother.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.270
Let's see it.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.722
- [Mario] You ready to find
out what you're having?

00:04:09.722 --> 00:04:11.508
- Yes, yes, I'm so scared.

00:04:11.508 --> 00:04:12.925
- You're having--

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.819
- Just tell us!

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:18.137
- [Mario] A little brother!

00:04:18.137 --> 00:04:19.419
(squeals)

00:04:19.419 --> 00:04:20.669
- Having a boy.

00:04:22.309 --> 00:04:23.807
Yes, I'm the queen.

00:04:23.807 --> 00:04:25.583
- [Mario] You're the queen.

00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:27.320
You can still protect her,

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:30.158
you can still protect your little brother.

00:04:30.158 --> 00:04:31.908
- Yes, I'm the queen.

00:04:33.543 --> 00:04:34.376
(audience clapping)

00:04:34.376 --> 00:04:37.369
What she got from that
is, I have no competition.

00:04:37.369 --> 00:04:38.330
That's what she got.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.457
- Exactly, no one's going
to be borrowing her clothes.

00:04:40.457 --> 00:04:41.417
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:04:41.417 --> 00:04:43.563
- You know we waited on
all three of the kids

00:04:43.563 --> 00:04:45.610
to find out what we were having.

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.380
It took some convincing
initially with my wife.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.265
But then she loved it.

00:04:48.265 --> 00:04:50.893
You're excited. It's either a boy or girl.

00:04:50.893 --> 00:04:51.740
It's not like, "oh, it's a monkey".

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.610
It's not a real big surprise.
- It's a fifty-fifty.

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.140
- You still get a euphoric feeling.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:59.370
And we didn't tell the kids either

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.390
until we got home from the hospital.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.993
So that's when I recorded them.

00:05:03.921 --> 00:05:05.876
It was fun.
- Oh my gosh that's sweet.

00:05:05.876 --> 00:05:06.709
- Anybody pregnant out there it's awesome

00:05:06.709 --> 00:05:07.655
to wait by the way.

00:05:07.655 --> 00:05:09.116
Its awesome to wait.

00:05:09.116 --> 00:05:10.353
- Anyone pregnant out
there I'm just sorry,

00:05:10.353 --> 00:05:12.215
I mean I'm happy for you, but I'm sorry.

00:05:12.215 --> 00:05:14.267
You probably feel horrible it's great.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.550
They're great when they
come out you'll love it.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:19.300
Are Gia and Nico helping
out with the new baby?

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.775
- Yeah, they're obsessed
with the baby right now.

00:05:20.775 --> 00:05:25.304
And Gia, she's only 8, but she's
such a great little helper.

00:05:25.304 --> 00:05:27.860
It's like I have a little
nanny that I don't have to pay.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:28.869
It's great.

00:05:28.869 --> 00:05:31.270
She'll feed him, she'll take care.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.710
And then my son Dominic can't wait

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.380
to start taking him to
wrestling, jiu jitsu.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:38.670
If it was up to me I'd keep having them.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:41.581
My wife says, hey you can
keep having them, but--

00:05:41.581 --> 00:05:44.277
But I love it. I like the
chaos, you know we have the dog,

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.790
the kids, everybody running around.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:46.623
So I like it.

00:05:46.623 --> 00:05:48.250
- I like a big family too.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.410
I think cause I grew
up not with my family.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.528
I was only really with my mom.

00:05:51.528 --> 00:05:53.210
So it's like I didn't
grow up around my brothers

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.737
and sisters and that's
why I love it so much

00:05:54.737 --> 00:05:56.140
right now with ours.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:56.973
And I want more.

00:05:56.973 --> 00:05:59.081
And my husband is like, "No".

00:05:59.081 --> 00:06:00.650
Cause we have four.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.059
But you're kids are also
on your radio show too.

00:06:02.059 --> 00:06:03.660
You involve them at work right?

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:04.931
- Yeah, well I do the show
with my wife actually.

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:07.010
"On With Mario", by the way,

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.432
if you're interested in checking it out.

00:06:08.432 --> 00:06:09.795
Its cool.

00:06:09.795 --> 00:06:11.200
I love working with her.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.530
She only comes a couple days a week

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:13.651
and we bank the segments.

00:06:13.651 --> 00:06:15.967
She'd probably kill me if I had
to sit everyday right there.

00:06:15.967 --> 00:06:18.238
But it's fun we got the
whole family in on the act.

00:06:18.238 --> 00:06:21.100
The kids, oh she's interviewing
I think Adam Levine

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.133
in that particular clip right there.

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:24.377
She loves Maroon 5.

00:06:24.377 --> 00:06:27.330
But my kids also do movie reviews.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:30.193
And if they're rated R then
they just watch the trailer.

00:06:31.515 --> 00:06:33.433
Then they do unseen movie reviews.

00:06:33.433 --> 00:06:35.030
It's pretty funny.

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:35.910
- I wanna see them do
movie reviews of rated R.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.840
- But Gias has done red
carpets, interviewed everyone

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:41.241
from The Rock to Ellen, to everyone.

00:06:41.241 --> 00:06:42.140
- What? Okay.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:42.973
That's amazing.

00:06:42.973 --> 00:06:44.020
So Gia also has...

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:44.853
I love Gia.

00:06:44.853 --> 00:06:46.524
Gia also has a side hustle I'm aware of.

00:06:46.524 --> 00:06:48.672
She sells her drawings.

00:06:48.672 --> 00:06:50.333
- She's a little entrepreneur.

00:06:51.492 --> 00:06:52.325
She likes to sell her little artwork.

00:06:52.325 --> 00:06:53.878
And she negotiates everything.

00:06:53.878 --> 00:06:57.370
And so we're running a
studio one day or something.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.860
- Well there is one piece of
artwork that I really, really

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:01.180
love that I want to get to.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:03.250
The tooth fairy thing I saw,
I think it was on Instagram.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:07.827
This letter is magical and
I want us to put it up.

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:08.820
"Dear Tooth Fairy,

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.400
Over the years you have given me money

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.984
because I have given you my teeth.

00:07:11.984 --> 00:07:16.984
This year I would kindly ask
you if I could keep my teeth.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:20.330
Please circle Yes or No."

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.163
And then she hearts Yes.

00:07:23.318 --> 00:07:24.818
And then she says, "thank
you for your generosity

00:07:24.818 --> 00:07:26.890
over the past years".

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:28.320
She is very polite.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.153
- Very polite.

00:07:29.153 --> 00:07:29.986
- I love her.

00:07:29.986 --> 00:07:31.920
- I always say manners are so important.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.122
I teach my kids the most important words

00:07:33.122 --> 00:07:36.290
are please, thank you, you're
welcome, and excuse me.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.123
- That's very Southern as well.

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:38.373
- So I won't answer them unless they start

00:07:38.373 --> 00:07:39.363
with that sentence.

00:07:40.739 --> 00:07:41.572
But yeah, she was trying
to basically hit her up

00:07:41.572 --> 00:07:42.405
for more money.

